Do not report a failed result fetch as a successful measurement.

VL53LX_GetMultiRangingData() assigns SetMeasurementData()'s return value over
VL53LX_get_device_results()'s, so a fetch that failed part-way through is handed
back as VL53LX_ERROR_NONE. Two consequences, and the second is the dangerous one.

The caller receives a status that says the measurement is good. What the output
actually holds is whatever VL53LX_get_device_results() managed to write before it
failed: VL53LX_f_025() writes the new result__stream_count at its entry
(vl53lx_hist_algos_gen4.c), presults->active_results++ is not guarded by status
(ibid.), and VL53LX_get_device_results() copies the results out unconditionally
(vl53lx_api_core.c). So a slot counted as active but never filled by VL53LX_f_017()
is indistinguishable from a real target, and it arrives carrying an ADVANCED stream
count -- which defeats a consumer's replay guard, because the guard's whole basis is
that a repeated count means a repeated frame.

And SetMeasurementData() runs anyway, which updates pdev->PreviousStreamCount from
the histogram data. The device's own stream history therefore moves on a fetch that
failed, so the next comparison is made against a count that no successful read ever
produced.

Guarding the call fixes both: the original error survives, and the bookkeeping that
would have hidden it does not run. Nothing else changes -- on the success path the
sequence is byte-for-byte what it was.

This is a fail-closed change. A caller that used to get a plausible distance from a
failed fetch now gets an error and no sample, which for a cliff sensor is the only
safe direction: reporting four-seconds-stale floor as the floor now is the failure
this driver must not have.

Reported by review on PR #98 (2026-08-24, re-stated 2026-09-17). Applied to a copy
in the build directory, never in place, so SHA256SUMS keeps answering whether
upstream itself was edited.

--- a/modules/vl53lx_api.c
+++ b/modules/vl53lx_api.c
@@ -1049,7 +1049,8 @@
 				VL53LX_DEVICERESULTSLEVEL_FULL,
 				presults);
 
-	Status = SetMeasurementData(Dev,
+	if (Status == VL53LX_ERROR_NONE)
+		Status = SetMeasurementData(Dev,
 					presults,
 					pMultiRangingData);
 
